  "language": "en",
  "text": "Track 5.1 Good afternoon everyone. Thank you for coming My name is Karen Smith, and I'm here from the Future Advice Centre Next year you finish school, so it's time to think about what you want to do next There are some important things for you to think about and today We're going to talk about jobs and for those of you who want to go to university choosing a subject to study The first thing you need to ask yourself is do I want to leave school next year or Do I want to go to university? You don't have to go to university If you want to work in a restaurant, I think it's better to work and learn at the same time A chef can teach you how to cook and you get good experience Another thing to remember is that the job doesn't have to pay very well Choose a job you enjoy Many creative people like musicians don't earn much, but they often have fun Do you want a job where you help people for example as a doctor or nurse? They work long hours, but their jobs are interesting Whatever job you do you should have time to relax and enjoy your life It's good to see friends and watch TV You should talk to your parents, too They can also give you advice about jobs, but remember it's your life and your future",
